<h2>Why Arm Length Changes Everything</h2>
<p>Two players who are both exactly 6'0" can have standing reaches that differ by 4 to 6 inches depending on their arm length. That difference translates directly into how high they need to jump to dunk — a player with a 6'6" wingspan at 6'0" has a dramatically easier time dunking than a player with a 5'10" wingspan at the same height.</p>
<table class="data-table">
<thead>
<tr>
